class	equivocation
word	be
fault	"no longer to be what he is" is ceasing to be ignorant, a thing he is in some respect; "not to be" is ceasing to exist
reference	Aristotle, Sophistical Refutations 5, 166b37-167a20 (what is said simply and in some respect)
known	canon
